      "writtenOn": "2024-05-01T18:14:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I checked with people more experienced with the block layer and their feedback is:\n\nblkdev_get_by_path() should be used in the zram driver. Using struct file or any file API when accessing a block device is wrong. They should submit bio\u0027s directly to the block device. There are multiple examples in the out-of-tree SCST project. SCST is a collection of kernel drivers that exports local storage via a SCSI-over-network protocol. Source code is available at https://github.com/SCST-project/. See also the scst/src/dev_handlers/scst_vdisk.c file in that project. We also have an open request to upstream the change for ZRAM driver to use blkdev_get_by_path() in  https://b.corp.google.com/issues/195421698 (might not be accessible for partners).",
      "parentUuid": "5f1a081b_1a23fea3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 494,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 511,
        "endChar": 17
